% Non-coding computer time: work / study / brain rot; what stood out.
\p{Non-coding computer time is back: the arbtt capture log had silently corrupted and I have since recovered it. The week turned out research-heavy — of the 25.8 hours tracked, most is \strong{Work}: papers and ML-systems reading, roughly 18 hours of it. A title-only tracker had been mis-filing that reading as the unclassifiable residual, so the honest \strong{Other} is about a quarter (5.9h), and it is mostly personal browsing — shopping, recipes, the odd job application — not work I bounced off. Still worth clawing back. The pomodoro method is the fix: pick one thing and do not diverge \strong{for anything} until the timer ends.}
